{"id": "tea:rudrahrdaya-upanisad:1-5", "source": "src:rudrahrdaya-upanisad", "location": {"ref": "1-5"}, "paraphrase": "Śuka asks Vyāsa which god is the self of all gods; Vyāsa: Rudra; Umā is Viṣṇu; one who bows to Govinda bows to Śaṅkara; one who hates Virūpākṣa hates Janārdana; the union of Umā and Śaṅkara is Viṣṇu.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:siva-visnu-identity"], "disputes": ["dsp:which-deity-is-supreme"], "teachers": ["tch:suka", "tch:vyasa"], "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "verification": {"level": "sourced", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": [{"phase": "C", "date": "2026-09-29", "method": "text-locate", "queries": ["e-text rudrahrdaya-upanisad 1-5"], "evidence": ["catalog:raw_etexts:108_Upanishads", "text:sources_raw/raw_etexts/vedaH/misc/upaniShat/mixedPF/108_Upanishads.md"], "result": "confirmed", "note": "Śuka's question to Vyāsa and the answer 'Rudra; Umā is Viṣṇu' are in e-text vv. 1-5, after an unnumbered maṅgala. The Govinda/Śaṅkara and Virūpākṣa/Janārdana verses are vv. 6-7.", "by": "sourcing:U04-minor-upanisads"}]}, "coverage": ["A2"], "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U04-minor-upanisads"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
